<title>USA: Gibson Q3 includes charge, tax benefit.</title>
<headline>Gibson Q3 includes charge, tax benefit.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gibson Greetings Inc said Thursday it took a $2.1 million charge and had a $3.7 million tax benefit in the third quarter from the liquidation of its Mexican subsidiary.</p>
<p>As a result of the liquidation of Gibson de Mexico SA de CV, net income rose $1.6 million, or $0.10 per share, it said.</p>
<p>For the quarter, the company today reported net income of $4.1 million, or $0.25 per share, versus pro forma net income of $1.9 million, or $0.12 per share, a year earlier.</p>
</text>
